3
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:14,100
We identified three main problems
in the traditional workbook market.

4
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:17,317
First, simply moving paper
workbooks to tablets

5
00:00:17,373 --> 00:00:19,870
did not demonstrate
better learning results.

6
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:24,590
Second, sales pressure without
effective tools led to teacher burnout.

7
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:29,570
Third, vague messages about study habits
failed to address parents' concerns.

8
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:34,510
JEI must address two strategic enemies.

9
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:39,820
The first is repetitive math drills that
focus on speed rather than understanding.

10
00:00:40,270 --> 00:00:44,440
The second is tablet-based learning
that relies too much on gamification.

11
00:00:44,990 --> 00:00:47,633
Instead, JEI aims to
help students understand

12
00:00:47,691 --> 00:00:50,510
their mistakes and solve
problems independently.

13
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:57,430
Competitors often focus on more content,
repetitive drills, and heavy advertising.

14
00:00:57,880 --> 00:01:00,190
JEI will take a different approach.

15
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:05,290
Through precise assessment, personalized
step-by-step learning, and independent

16
00:01:05,349 --> 00:01:09,410
problem-solving, we aim to give
parents a clear reason to choose JEI.

17
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:14,000
This can help keep current students and
attract new students through referrals.

18
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:19,060
Our positioning is "Thinking-Focused
Diagnostic Learning."

19
00:01:19,510 --> 00:01:23,310
Our Verbal Nail is "A Child Who
Understands Why They Got It Wrong."

20
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:29,120
Our Visual Hammer is the "Defect
Linker," based on 12,759 error patterns.

21
00:01:29,670 --> 00:01:32,351
Our goal is to help
students discover solutions

22
00:01:32,408 --> 00:01:35,260
on their own, rather than
simply memorize answers.

23
00:01:37,010 --> 00:01:40,180
We also need to change how
we communicate with parents.

24
00:01:40,630 --> 00:01:43,637
Instead of focusing on general
study habits, we highlight

25
00:01:43,690 --> 00:01:46,170
a child's ability to
understand their mistakes.

26
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:51,300
The Defect Linker shows the causes of
learning gaps through a simple visual map.

27
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:55,900
This helps parents understand their
child's learning needs and builds trust.

28
00:01:57,650 --> 00:02:00,070
We will focus on two main target groups.

29
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:04,440
First, children aged six to seven
preparing for elementary school.

30
00:02:04,890 --> 00:02:07,388
We offer precise assessment
and step-by-step

31
